    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: I have reviewed the whole record and I decide as follows.\n\nThe SGD 8.00 no-show fee stands, and the driver is owed SGD 6.40.\n\nWHY THE FEE STANDS. POL-NS-01 requires four things of the driver, and all four are met. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 16:02:25 on 30 July. (b) The GPS trace — unbroken, 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps — puts the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 16:02:10, fifteen seconds before that marker, with 60 qualifying fixes, so the arrival geofence test under POL-NS-02 is satisfied. (c) The dwell is measured from that first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the tap, and runs continuously to 16:11:55 — 585 seconds against the 300-second minimum for this zone class. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 16:12:10, after the required dwell had elapsed at 16:07:10, with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which is one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, and there is no boarding event anywhere in the record.\n\nWHY NO RIDER-SIDE CLAUSE DISPLACES IT. POL-NS-06 needs a waiting-period shortfall; there is none — the measured dwell exceeds the minimum by 285 seconds, and the rider does not contest this. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the 16:02:25 marker the driver was already stationary inside the arrival radius at 0 km/h, so the marker is not a false-arrival event and there is no referral to record under POL-NS-05(ii). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider because limb (b) fails outright: the driver replied to her 16:08:02 message at 16:08:20, 18 seconds later, and placed an answered 34-second in-app call at 16:09:40. POL-NS-03 is not engaged: it concerns a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m, and this driver held position inside the radius.\n\nTWO POINTS THE RIDER RAISES, BOTH ACCEPTED, NEITHER CHANGING THE OUTCOME. First, she correctly says the rider's distance from the pin is not an element of the charge and must not be weighed as though it were; her track (141 fixes, none qualifying inside the 150 m presence radius, 633.9 m at closest) answers none of the four conditions, and I do not weigh it against her. Second, nothing may be built on the absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00208-01 (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT): a missing artifact carries no fact, and no accumulation of in-geofence intervals under POL-NS-06(i) is needed or made, because the driver's time in the geofence is a single unbroken run.\n\nON THE PROFILES. No ground of decision and no escalation is built from either profile. prior_no_show_flags (3) is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 marks context-only and may not be substituted for the trailing-window figure it resembles; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the POL-NS-09(d) threshold of 3, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both sides, so POL-NS-09(c) is not engaged.\n\nDRIVER COMPENSATION. Because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80% of the SGD 8.00 fee, being SGD 6.40. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2/143 = 0.014 (below 0.08). Both limbs must fail before compensation is withheld; neither does. The fee itself is correctly itemised: under fee_schedule.resolution_rule the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 8.00 RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee is SGD 8.00, exactly the line charged, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged.\n\nPer POL-GEN-03 this ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION: the rider's charge stands and the platform pays the driver SGD 6.40; amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd and is the amount this ruling moves, not a refund to the filing party.\n\nCONFIDENCE. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the trip record, the GPS trace and the chat log — sits at weight_multiplier 1.0, and no limb (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08 is met (no clock skew beyond 90 seconds, no sampling gap, no missing or truncated chat, and the fee reconciles exactly). Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation arises.",
